{
  "_comment": [
    "US coinage composition -- public facts, seedable from mint specifications.",
    "Composition is a matter of legislation, so it resolves from what the coin",
    "is rather than being recorded per item. A dime struck in 1963 is 90%",
    "silver because the law said so, not because anyone typed it in.",
    "",
    "A row names a denomination, a design series, or both. A row with a series",
    "is that design's own and outranks the denomination's row: a Morgan dollar",
    "of 2021 is .999 silver, a Sacagawea dollar of that year is brass-clad, and",
    "a commemorative dollar of 1986 is 90% silver, though all three are dollar",
    "coins. A bullion design with one size names only its series; one struck in",
    "several sizes has a row per face value. The denomination's row is every",
    "other coin's of that face value and year.",
    "",
    "fine_weight_ozt is the published ASW (actual silver weight) where one",
    "exists, not a recomputation from gross weight -- the published figure is",
    "what the market quotes and what every dealer's calculator agrees with.",
    "A weight the Coinage Acts set in grains is the statute's figure over 480,",
    "a troy ounce being 480 grains.",
    "",
    "A span has a row only where every coin of it shares one composition. A",
    "dollar of 1971-1976 was struck in copper-nickel clad for circulation and in",
    "40% silver for collectors, and a five-cent piece of 1942 and a cent of",
    "1864 or 1982 in two alloys each, so none of them has a row: the weight of such a",
    "coin is entered by hand. For the",
    "same reason the years a standard changed in -- 1837, 1853, 1873 -- are",
    "left out where both standards were struck, and a commemorative dollar",
    "has a row only through 2018, after which one was struck at five ounces.",
    "",
    "A row naming a set form describes only the coins issued in that set:",
    "the dime, quarter and half dollar of a Silver Proof Set from 1992 are",
    "silver though every other coin of their face value and year is clad,",
    "and so are the 1976 silver set's quarter, half and dollar. A coin is",
    "read by them only when it is recorded in that set; a proof with no set",
    "recorded, in those years, could be either, so the metal recorded on it",
    "chooses, and with none it has no composition.",
    "",
    "This is exactly the kind of table a new installation should inherit rather",
    "than rebuild: nothing here is specific to one collection."
  ],
